# Line endings: LF in the repository and LF in every checkout, whatever the
# machine's core.autocrlf says. On Windows, autocrlf turned every text file
# into CRLF on checkout, so a zip built there carried CRLF files, and the build
# stamp, a hash over the bytes of the .py files, came out different from the
# one built on the server from the same commit. With this the release zip is
# the same byte for byte wherever it is built.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever their content looks like.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.gpkg binary
*.qgz binary
